    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Beautiful detached 3-bedroom home in superb location within walking distance of Foxford town and all its fantastic amenities. Situated in a superb and highly convenient location within walking distance of Foxford town centre, this spacious and three-bedroom detached home offers comfortable accommodation and excellent access to local amenities and transport links. \r\n\r\nThe property comprises an entrance hallway, three bedrooms, sitting room, kitchen/dining/living room, two shower rooms and hotpress. A newly installed ramp leads to the front door, while a driveway extends to the side of the property providing ample parking and access to the convenient detached garage located to the rear. The property includes a rear garden also which is not overlooked. \r\n\r\nThe property is ideally positioned for convenient travel and local amenities, with the bus stop just a five-minute walk away, offering regular services to major towns and cities. Foxford Train Station is less than a five-minute drive, while Ireland West Airport Knock is also just 25 minutes away. \r\n\r\nFamilies will appreciate the proximity of both Foxford National School and St. Joseph’s Secondary School, each within a five-minute walk. The larger towns of Ballina (15km), Swinford (12km) and Castlebar (28km) are also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nFoxford itself is a bustling village offering a wonderful range of amenities, including shops, bars, restaurants, a library, and the iconic Foxford Woollen Mills. \r\n\r\nNestled on the banks of the River Moy with Ox Mountain as its backdrop, the town is surrounded by beautiful countryside, with Lough Conn, Pontoon beaches and scenic walking trails including the Foxford Way, Shanwar Belgarrow and Larganmore Loop Walks all on the doorstep.\r\n\r\nThis is an ideal home for those seeking a welcoming and vibrant community, convenience, and the beauty of the Mayo countryside."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway \r\n10.36m (34'0\") x 1.72m (5'8\")\r\nThe front door has a side panel providing natural light into the hall which has a carpet floor.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room \r\n8.12m (26'8\") x 4.56m (15'0\")\r\nBright room with lino flooring, fitted kitchen with tiled splashback and two large windows providing ample natural light. A door leads outside to the side of the property.\r\n\r\nSitting Room \r\n3.83m (12'7\") x 4.54m (14'11\")\r\nBright room to the front of the house with a carpet floor, open fireplace, and large window providing natural light.\r\n\r\nShower Room \r\n3.22m (10'7\") x 1.88m (6'2\")\r\nWith a lino floor, pedestal sink, toilet, and shower. A window provides natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \r\n3.28m (10'9\") x 4.55m (14'11\")\r\nDouble room to the front of the property with a carpet floor, built-in wardrobe with vanity unit, and a large window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\n2.94m (9'8\") x 2.68m (8'10\")\r\nDouble room to the side of the property with a carpet floor, built-in wardrobe, and a large window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 \r\n3m (9'10\") x 97m (318'3\")\r\nDouble room to the rear of the property with a carpet floor, built-in wardrobe with vanity unit, and a large window overlooking the rear garden.\r\n\r\nShower Room 2 \r\n2.65m (8'8\") x 2.27m (7'5\")\r\nFully tiled with a floating wash hand basin, toilet, and wet-room shower. A window provides natural light and ventilation."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious three-bedroom detached home\r\nSuperb location within walking distance of Foxford town centre\r\nNew ramp providing easy access to the front door\r\nDetached garage offering excellent additional storage\r\nGenerous driveway with ample off-street parking\r\nPrivate rear garden, not overlooked\r\nExcellent transport links, including nearby bus and train services\r\nIreland West Airport Knock just 25 minutes away\r\nFantastic amenities nearby including shops, restaurants, bars, library\r\nHome to the iconic Foxford Woollen Mills"
      },
